# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for `make cpp-tsan`.
#
# Arrow and Parquet are prebuilt without instrumentation, so ThreadSanitizer
# cannot see the synchronization inside them: the guard that makes a
# function-local static thread-safe, and the atomic compare-and-swap that
# publishes a cached fingerprint, both run in code it does not observe, while
# the std::string and std::shared_ptr code touching the same memory comes from
# our instrumented objects. Arrow documents its types as immutable and safe to
# share across threads. Each entry names one such mechanism inside Arrow;
# none matches our own functions, so a race between two accesses in our own
# code is still reported.

# Type and field fingerprints, computed lazily and published atomically.
race:arrow::detail::Fingerprintable
race:ComputeFingerprint

# Function-local statics initialized on first use by whichever worker gets
# there first: Arrow's type singletons (arrow::binary()::result and its
# siblings) and Parquet's writer-version constants.
race:arrow::*()::result
race:arrow::TypeTraits
race:parquet::ApplicationVersion

# A type singleton is a heap block that std::make_shared allocates inside the
# static's initializer, so a report on one names that block, which the entries
# above do not match, and the constructor that wrote it, which this one does.
# A type that this package makes and hands to another thread without
# synchronization is still reported, on the std::shared_ptr that carries it;
# the race on the type's own fields is not.
race:arrow::DataType::DataType

# Parquet's default reader and writer properties, first-use statics as well:
# parquet::default_reader_properties(), default_writer_properties(),
# default_arrow_reader_properties() and default_arrow_writer_properties().
race:parquet::default_
